    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule now extends to public holidays. I updated `BusinessDayResolver.toBusinessDay` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDayResolver.java`) \u2014 the single place that already owned this logic and is called from `OwnerRestControllerV1` when normalizing the registration date.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added the fixed holiday set (`2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`).\n- Replaced the weekend-only \"jump to next Monday\" logic with a roll-forward loop that advances one day while the date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday. This correctly handles chains where rolling off a holiday lands on a weekend (or vice versa) \u2014 e.g. Fri 2026-12-25 (holiday) \u2192 Sat/Sun \u2192 Mon 2026-12-28 (holiday) \u2192 Tue 2026-12-29.\n- Extracted a small `isWeekend` helper to keep the loop condition readable.\n\nThis mirrors the algorithm the acceptance tests replicate (`AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`), and keeps the resolver as the one small unit responsible for this rule. `mvnw test` reports BUILD SUCCESS with no failures.",
